      "message": "I think this should be something like \"setMatchHostCpuTopology\"\n\nIf we have this, I\u0027m not sure we should keep numCpus (especially since I believe it requires setting nVCpus \u003d\u003d nRealCpus).\n\nHow about we offer 2 options:\n- 1 vCPU (probably the default)\n- Match host CPU topology.\n\nAre there any other options that could be selected without detailed knowledge of the device and extreme tuning, with an API that mere mortals can understand?\n\nWe could perhaps expose more sophisticated options via the JSON config for platform-specific code.\n\nChanging the CPU topology shouldn\u0027t invalidate VM identity, I thing.",
